  "text": "marta (Design): Quick design review \u2014 Invite modal when Org SSO is ON. Current disabled role dropdown shows 'Role (SSO enforced)'. Feels ambiguous, users might think roles are removed entirely. Screenshot: https://redwood.app/s/shot123 :eyes:\najay (PM): +1, saw a support ticket where someone thought they lost admin rights because they couldn't change the role during invite. Need clearer copy and discoverable path to manage roles via IdP.\nev an (FE): re: implementation \u2014 right now we render <select disabled> with a tooltip. Can swap to a read-only field easily but need UX copy first. Also need to ensure keyboard focus doesn't land on a disabled control.\nkim (A11y): flagged: tooltips on hover are not accessible by keyboard. If we rely on a tooltip to explain SSO-managed roles, we need a focusable element (button or link) with aria-describedby. Also ensure color contrast for the muted helper text.\nmarta (Design): proposal: replace disabled select with a read-only row: 'Roles controlled by SSO' + info icon that opens a small dialog with: \"Roles are managed by your organization\u2019s SSO provider. To change default role for new invites, update provisioning rules or contact your IdP admin.\" + link to docs. Copy suggestion: \"Roles managed by SSO \u2014 manage via your identity provider\" (short).\najay (PM): Sounds good. Add an inline CTA to 'View provisioning docs' rather than 'contact admin' to reduce support tickets. Prioritize for 1.26.\nevan (FE): sample attrs I'll use for the info button: ```html\n<button aria-label=\\\"Roles managed by SSO \u2014 more info\\\" aria-haspopup=\\\"dialog\\\">i</button>\n<div role=\\\"dialog\\\" aria-modal=\\\"false\\\" id=\\\"sso-roles-help\\\">...content...</div>\n```\nI'll make sure the button is tabbable and the dialog gets focus on open. Need the final copy for the dialog and the docs URL.\nkim (A11y): please ensure the dialog has role=dialog + aria-labelledby and a visible close button. If it's a non-modal tooltip alternative, use role=region and aria-live=\\\"polite\\\" so screen readers announce it but don't trap users. Also verify contrast and focus styles.\nmarta (Design): updated copy for dialog header: 'SSO-managed roles' and body: 'Your org controls which roles invitees receive. To change defaults, update role mappings in your identity provider. See provisioning docs.' Link text: 'SSO provisioning docs'.\najay (PM): thanks \u2014 evan can you add a small inline note under the email field: 'Invited users will receive the role defined by SSO' (muted, 12px) \u2014 avoid all-caps.\nevan (FE): will do. Quick question: should we show the actual role name (e.g., \"Member\") if the IdP provides it, or is that too risky?\nmarta (Design): prefer not to show a dynamic role from IdP in modal for now \u2014 confusing edge cases. Keep it generic. We can explore showing a mapping preview in a follow-up.\nkim (A11y): once implemented i'll run a quick axe sweep. Also request a keyboard-only UX check before we ship.\ndeploy-bot: build 1.26.2-preview deployed to staging at 2026-03-23T14:07Z :rocket:\najay (PM): great \u2014 schedule a short QA pass tomorrow, then ship in canary. Thanks everyone :thumbsup:\nmarta (Design): TY all, I'll drop updated mock and link to the staging flow in the ticket.",
